No, your roomie is *not* the first. I discovered this phenomenon
accidentally when I was "tricked" once, and noticed all these
"Levels.X" files on the disk I had inadvertantly not inserted back.
Out of curiosity, I discovered that if you start a game on one disk,
drop a pile of items one level up or down, trick yourself, restart
with a copy of the same game on a different disk, switch disks, and
save, you duplicate everything you carted up or down the stairs. (I
play on an Atari ST).

> That's right, you can clone stuff -- any stuff -- ad nauseam.
